    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Topline Character Counter adds a live character and word counter to the Gutenberg editor toolbar.</p>\n<p>It displays:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Total number of characters</li>\n<li>Number of characters without spaces</li>\n<li>Number of words</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The counter updates automatically while you edit your post.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Install and activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Open a post or page in the Gutenberg editor.</li>\n<li>The character and word counter will appear in the top editor toolbar.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"will%20it%20slow%20down%20my%20editor%3F\">\nWill it slow down my editor?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. The plugin uses lightweight JavaScript and WordPress hooks.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20work%20with%20gutenberg%3F\">\nDoes it work with Gutenberg?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. The plugin is designed specifically for the Gutenberg block editor.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
